From 9df39118b14582f5a46be90b292956413e40d179 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MaiRat <enrico.bartky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 09:24:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run async and generator bodies under the strict-mode runtime
 flag

An async or generator body runs during its rewritten driver's steps, not during
the JSFunction.InvokeFunction call that created it, so it never inherited the
EnterStrictMode scope ordinary calls establish. A failing [[Set]] inside a
'use strict' async/generator body therefore did not throw (it silently did
nothing), even in the async function's synchronous prefix or a generator before
its first yield; and a strict async function's "this" was coerced to the global
object instead of left undefined.

ClrGeneratorV2 now carries the function's strict flag and re-enters it around
each body step (its Next), so the body observes strict [[Set]] semantics on
every step and across yields/awaits. The compiler sets IsStrictMode on the
generator and on the async function's inner generator, and passes
coerceThis:!isStrictFunction to the async inner generator so a strict async
function's "this" is left undefined.

Updates the StrictModeFlowTests KnownGap test (which pinned the old no-throw
behaviour) to assert TypeError, and adds Track1LanguageTests regressions,
including sloppy-body guards. BuiltIns 2214 green, Integration 5032 of 5033
(pre-existing M8 only).
